{"name":"Nuthatch Back","hex":"#445599","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"nuthatch","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various small passerine birds from the genus Sitta, found throughout the northern hemisphere and noted for their unusual proclivity for climbing down trees head first."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nuthatch"},{"term":"back","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["At or near the rear.","Returned or restored to a previous place or condition."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["To or in a previous condition or place.","In a direction opposite to that in which someone or something is facing or normally pointing."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/back"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nuthatch","blocks":[{"text":"The nuthatches constitute a genus, Sitta, of small passerine birds belonging to the family Sittidae. Characterised by large heads, short tails, and powerful bills and feet, nuthatches advertise their territory using loud, simple songs. Most species exhibit grey or bluish upper parts and a black eye stripe."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Sitta_europaea_-Rouge_Cloitre_estate%2C_Sonian_Forest%2C_near_Brussels%2C_Belgium-8.jpg/330px-Sitta_europaea_-Rouge_Cloitre_estate%2C_Sonian_Forest%2C_near_Brussels%2C_Belgium-8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nuthatch","wikidata":"Q858577"},{"title":"Human back","blocks":[{"text":"The human back, also called the dorsum, is the large posterior area of the human body, rising from the top of the buttocks to the back of the neck. It is the surface of the body opposite from the chest and the abdomen. The vertebral column runs the length of the back and creates a central area of recession. The breadth of the back is created by the shoulders at the top and the pelvis at the bottom."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Posterior_view_of_human_female_and_male_backs_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Posterior_view_of_human_female_and_male_backs_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Human_back","wikidata":"Q133279"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Red-breasted-Nuthatch-3c.jpg/500px-Red-breasted-Nuthatch-3c.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Red-breasted-Nuthatch-3c.jpg/1280px-Red-breasted-Nuthatch-3c.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Red-breasted-Nuthatch-3c.jpg/500px-Red-breasted-Nuthatch-3c.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The red-breasted nuthatch is said to have a callⓘ like a tin trumpet.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARed-breasted-Nuthatch-3c.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/White-cheeked_Nuthatch_%28Sitta_leucopsis%29_%2839661424053%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-White-cheeked_Nuthatch_%28Sitta_leucopsis%29_%2839661424053%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/White-cheeked_Nuthatch_%28Sitta_leucopsis%29_%2839661424053%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-White-cheeked_Nuthatch_%28Sitta_leucopsis%29_%2839661424053%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWhite-cheeked_Nuthatch_(Sitta_leucopsis)_(39661424053)_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Przevalski%27s_nuthatch_-_Chengdong_Wang_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Przevalski%27s_nuthatch_-_Chengdong_Wang_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_so